response:
 The expression \(\frac{\sqrt[4]{7}}{\sqrt[3]{7}}\) can be rewritten as \(7^{\frac{1}{4}} \div 7^{\frac{1}{3}}\). Using the properties of exponents, we get \(7^{\frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{3}}\). The exponent \(\frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{3}\) can be calculated as follows: \[
\frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{3} = \frac{3}{12} - \frac{4}{12} = -\frac{1}{12}
\] So, the expression simplifies to \(7^{-\frac{1}{12}}\). Therefore, the value of the expression is \(7\) raised to the power of \(-\frac{1}{12}\). </think> <answer> \(-\frac{1}{12}\) </answer>

